Shape Area Calculation (Runtime Polymorphism)

Problem Statement:
Write a Java program to demonstrate method overriding and runtime polymorphism using shapes.

Create a parent class Shape with:

a method area() that returns 0

Create a subclass Rectangle with:

variables length and breadth

constructor to initialize these values

override area() to return the area of the rectangle

Create another subclass Circle with:

variable radius

constructor to initialize the radius

override area() to return the area of the circle

In the main() method:

create objects of Rectangle and Circle

store them using a Shape reference

print the area of each shape

Concepts tested: method overriding, runtime polymorphism, inheritance.